{"title":"Desert Wolf","html":"<article class=\"wp\"><div class=\"wp-main\"><p class=\"wp-lede\">A level 25 Desert Wolf that attacks with stab (melee).</p>\n      <h2>Fighting it</h2><div class=\"s\"><i>Weak</i> <span class=\"tag-chip weak\">slash</span></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">A weakness adds 15% damage (the game's own rule). Monsters have no resistances.</p>\n      <p class=\"s good\">⭐ Seen as an elite 2 times (0.9% of sightings). Elites have 3× HP, hit 1.4× harder, give 5× XP and 5× loot.</p>\n      <p class=\"s\">Special: packDamagePerAlly: .1</p>\n      <h2>Levels</h2><div class=\"q-picker\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Level\"><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/desert-wolf\">All levels</a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/desert-wolf?lv=24\">Lv 24 <span>11</span></a><a class=\"q-chip on\" href=\"#/monster/desert-wolf?lv=25\">Lv 25 <span>155</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/desert-wolf?lv=26\">Lv 26 <span>163</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/desert-wolf?lv=27\">Lv 27 <span>9</span></a></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">The same monster spawns at different levels, and its hitpoints, damage and XP follow its level (the game’s own formula). In the game a monster more than 5 levels above you shows its level as “???”.</p>\n      <div class=\"g-scroll\"><table class=\"g-table q-table\"><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>HP</th><th>Damage</th><th>XP</th><th>Elite (HP · dmg · XP)</th><th>Seen</th><th>Mostly</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"\" data-href=\"#/monster/desert-wolf?lv=24\" title=\"Pick level 24\"><td><b>24</b></td><td>84</td><td>17.7</td><td>1,200</td><td class=\"muted\">252 · 24.8 · 3,600</td><td>11</td><td>near <a href=\"#/map/place/Scorpion%20Pits\">Scorpion Pits</a></td></tr><tr class=\"q-row-on\" data-href=\"#/monster/desert-wolf\" title=\"Show all levels\"><td><b>25</b> <span class=\"muted\">(base)</span></td><td>89</td><td>18.3</td><td>1,250</td><td class=\"muted\">267 · 25.6 · 3,750</td><td>155</td><td>near <a 